  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Young African Leaders Initiative (YALI) - Six Degrees Poultry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Having secured ample space, Six Degrees has mobilized $3,000.00 from savings towards a poultry venture in Muranga County and currently on the second lot of 1000 broiler chicken having attained an 18.33% ROI on the first harvest. Their primary goal with this project is to document while building capacity to control diseases, improved feed efficiency, handling of waste, and proper sanitizing of the poultry house for consistent growth and scale up. The farm will serve as a practical demonstration site for target beneficiaries in the surrounding counties while providing the much needed working capital to finance Six Degrees regular operations. As a business, they seek to leverage on growing partnerships with small holder farmers in other counties to extend training and investments onto other nutrient dense value chains and to profit from value addition and market linkages with demand side actors.</narrative>
  </description>
